<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Zacatlán> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Zacatlán** (Template:IPA-es is a city and [municipal seat](:Municipal_seat) of [Zacatlán Municipality](:Zacatl%C3%A1n_Municipality) located in the [Sierra Norte de Puebla](:Sierra_Norte_de_Puebla) region of [Puebla](:Puebla) in central [Mexico](:Mexico). The area is known for its production of apples, other fruit, cider and fruit wines, which are promoted through the annual Feria de la Manzana and Festival de la Sidra. It is also home to the [Relojes Centenario](:Relojes_Centenario) company, the first clock factory in [Latin America](:Latin_America) and the builder of the city's double sided [flower clock](:Flower_clock) in the main square. The historic center of the city is filled with traditional houses with red tile roofs and Zacatlan was designated a “[Pueblo Mágico](:Pueblo_M%C3%A1gico)” in 2011. Outside of the city proper, there is a significant indigenous population, the [Piedras Encimadas Valley](:Piedras_Encimadas_Valley) with its rock formations and various waterfalls and ravines."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
