<http://dbpedia.org/resource/City_of_regional_significance_(Ukraine)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "City of regional significance (Ukrainian: місто обласного значення, misto oblasnoho znachennya) in Ukraine was a type of second-level administrative division or municipality, the other type being raions (districts). In the first-level division of oblasts, they were referred to as cities of oblast significance; in the first-level autonomous republic of Crimea, they were cities of republican significance. The designation was created with the introduction of oblasts in 1932. It was abolished in a 2020 reform that merged raions together and integrated the city municipalities into them."@en .
