<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Xırdalan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Xırdalan** (*Khyrdalan*) is a city, municipality and the capital of the [Absheron District](:Absheron_District) of [Azerbaijan](:Azerbaijan). It has a population of 95,200. Khyrdalan is home of country's biggest brewery *Baltika Baku*, previously known as Khyrdalan . A monument to [Egyptian president](:President_of_Egypt) [Hosni Mubarak](:Hosni_Mubarak) was erected in 2007 in the city. Similarly, a statue of [Heydar Aliyev](:Heydar_Aliyev) was erected in [Cairo](:Cairo) in 2008. In the wake of the [2011 Egyptian protests](:2011_Egyptian_revolution), the Azerbaijani opposition, led by the [Musavat Party](:Musavat), demanded the demolition of the statue, calling it a \"worship of idols\". On 8 June 2011, the statue was taken down following Mubarak's resignation.On 29 November 2006, the settlement gained city status after its approval by the [National Assembly of Azerbaijan](:National_Assembly_%28Azerbaijan%29).This [Azerbaijan](:Azerbaijan)-related article is a [stub](:Wikipedia%3AStub). You can help Wikipedia by [expanding it](//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=X%C4%B1rdalan&action=edit)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
