<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Los_Angeles_City_Council> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Los Angeles City Council is the legislative body of the City of Los Angeles. The council is composed of 15 members elected from single-member districts for four-year terms. The president of the council and the president 'pro tempore' are chosen by the council at the first regular meeting of the term (after June 30 in odd-numbered years until 2017 and the second Monday of December in even-numbered years beginning in 2020). An assistant president pro tempore is appointed by the President. As of 2020, council members receive an annual salary of $207,000 per year, which is among the highest city council salary in the nation."@en .
