<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Hosur_Municipal_Corporation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Hosur Municipal Corporation is the civic body governing city of Hosur in Indian state of Tamil Nadu. It was the 13th Municipal corporation in Tamilnadu established on 13th february 2019.It is headed by a Mayor, who presides over 45 councillors represents over 45 wards of the city, and it has adjoined with Mathigiri town panchayat, Zuzuvadi, Avalapalli and Mookandapalli village panchayat. is one of the major industial city in Tamilnadu and had a population of about 5.3 lakhs. The annual income revenue of this corporation is about 114 crores. Tamilnadu government has announced a master plan for Hosur to develop the infrastructure and expanding the city area for around 700 sq.km for its tremendous growth and growing population."@en .
