<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Contra_Costa_County,_California> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Contra Costa County (/ˌkɒntrə ˈkɒstə/; Contra Costa, Spanish for \"Opposite Coast\") is a county located in the U.S. state of California, in the East Bay of the San Francisco Bay Area. As of the 2020 United States Census, the population was 1,165,927. The county seat is Martinez. It occupies the northern portion of the East Bay region of the San Francisco Bay Area and is primarily suburban. The county's name refers to its position on the other side of the bay from San Francisco. Contra Costa County is included in the San Francisco–Oakland–Berkeley, CA Metropolitan Statistical Area."@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Concepción,_Tucumán> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Concepción is a city and the department seat of Chicligasta in Tucumán Province, Argentina. It is located 76 km south of the provincial capital San Miguel de Tucumán and has a population of 49,782 (2010 census [INDEC]). Due to its population and bustling commercial activity, the city is considered to be the second most important urban area in the province (the first one being the Greater San Miguel de Tucumán region), and the main one in southern Tucumán. \n* Bartolomé Mitre Square. \n* Commercial district. \n* 24 de Septiembre Street. \n* San Martín Avenue. \n* \n* v \n* t \n* e"@en .
