<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ocean_Springs,_Mississippi> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Ocean Springs is a city in Jackson County, Mississippi, United States, approximately 2 miles (3.2 km) east of Biloxi and west of Gautier. It is part of the Pascagoula, Mississippi Metropolitan Statistical Area. The population was 17,225 at the 2000 U.S. Census. As of the 2010 U.S. Census, the city of Ocean Springs had a population of 17,442. Ocean Springs was the home town of the late Walter Inglis Anderson, a nationally renowned painter and muralist who died in 1965 from lung cancer. The town plays host to several festivals, including its Peter Anderson Festival and The Herb Festival."@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Skamania_County,_Washington> <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/areaLand> "4,2890e+09"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> .
