<http://dbpedia.org/resource/List_of_building_types> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Examples of single-family detached house types include: \n* Bungalow \n* Central-passage house (North America) \n* Chattel house (Caribbean) \n* Cottage (various) \n* Courtyard house (various) \n* Konak (Asia) \n* Log house (various) \n* Mansion (various) \n* Housebarn (various) \n* Split level home (various) \n* Upper Lusatian house (Europe)"@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Los_Teques> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "[10°20′N 67°02′W﻿ / ﻿10.333°N 67.033°W﻿ / 10.333; -67.033](https://geohack.toolforge.org/geohack.php?pagename=Los_Teques&params=10_20_N_67_02_W_region:VE_type:city)**Los Teques**Template:IPA-es is the capital of the state of [Miranda](:Miranda_%28state%29) and the municipality of [Guaicaipuro Municipality](:Guaicaipuro_Municipality). It is located in the capital region of north-central Venezuela. More specifically, southwest of [Caracas](:Caracas), 10° 21' 00\" N latitude and 67° 02' 30\" W Greenwich, 1,169 m above sea level. It is located in the Cordillera de la Costa, on the banks of the Río San Pedro, la enciclopedia libre, descending from an area located in the northeast. According to the Office for National Statistics in 2016, Los Teques has a population of 252,242 people. The city is considered to be part of the agglomeration known as Greater Caracas."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sai_Baba_Boulevard> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Sai Baba Town** is an eco-friendly [township](:Township) located in [Boisar](:Boisar), Maharashtra. It is an integrated township project on 110 acres of land with industrial and residential plots, designed by the architect Rushikesh H."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
