<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Lava_Hot_Springs,_Idaho> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Lava Hot Springs** is a city along the [Portneuf River](:Portneuf_River_%28Idaho%29) in eastern [Bannock County](:Bannock_County%2C_Idaho), [Idaho](:Idaho), United States. It is part of the [Pocatello, Idaho metropolitan area](:Pocatello%2C_Idaho_metropolitan_area). The population was 407 at the [2010 census](:2010_United_States_Census), down from 521 in 2000. Located in the mountainous valley of the Portneuf River on the old route of the [Oregon Trail](:Oregon_Trail) and [California Trail](:California_Trail), the city has become a popular resort location, noted for its numerous [hot springs](:Hot_spring) amenable to bathing and a turbulent [inner tube](:Tubing_%28recreation%29) run through part of the town."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
