<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kyushu> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Kyushu (九州, Kyūshū, pronounced [kʲɯꜜːɕɯː], literally \"Nine Provinces\") is the third-largest island of Japan's five main islands and the most southerly of the four largest islands (i.e. excluding Okinawa). In the past, it has been known as Kyūkoku (九国, \"Nine Countries\"), Chinzei (鎮西, \"West of the Pacified Area\") and Tsukushi-no-shima (筑紫島, \"Island of Tsukushi\"). The historical regional name Saikaidō (西海道, lit. West Sea Circuit) referred to Kyushu and its surrounding islands. Kyushu has a land area of 36,782 square kilometres (14,202 sq mi) and a population of 14,311,224 in 2018."@en .
